---
import Policy from '../layouts/Policy.astro';
import OperatorContact from '../components/OperatorContact.astro';
import { operator } from '../data/policies';
const sections: [string, string][] = [
  ['controller', 'Who handles your information'],
  ['information', 'Information and purposes'],
  ['processing', 'Local, cloud and AI processing'],
  ['sharing', 'Standard readings and sharing'],
  ['providers', 'Service providers and recipients'],
  ['location', 'Where processing happens'],
  ['retention', 'Retention and deletion'],
  ['security', 'Security'],
  ['rights', 'Your choices and rights'],
  ['children', 'Children and policy updates'],
];
---

<Policy
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How information moves through PaperEnjoyer, why we use it and the choices available to you."
  path="/privacy"
  sections={sections}
>
  <div class="policy-callout">
    <p>
      Your library has a local copy, but PaperEnjoyer also provides cloud services. Account sync,
      cloud parsing, server-based AI reading and share links can send content off your device.
      Turning off library sync does not turn off those other features.
    </p>
  </div>
  <section id="controller">
    <h2>1. Who handles your information</h2>
    <p>
      The operator providing services under the name PaperEnjoyer is responsible for the personal
      information processed for our website and online services (the “controller”, where that term
      applies). Use the same email for support, privacy requests and refund assistance.
    </p>
    <OperatorContact />
    <p>
      The university is a correspondence location only. This policy covers PaperEnjoyer’s handling
      of information, not the separate practices of a publisher, model provider or other service you
      use independently.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="information">
    <h2>2. Information we use and why</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Account and sign-in information:</strong> account identifiers, email address,
        available profile details and authentication/session information. We use these to sign you
        in, associate your devices and library, secure access and respond to requests.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Library and research content:</strong> PDFs, paper metadata, extracted text and
        images, notes, annotations, selected conversation content, reading positions, folders and
        supported preferences. The features you use determine which items are processed locally,
        synchronized or sent for a task.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>AI and parsing requests:</strong> selected papers or passages, questions,
        instructions, relevant conversation context, generated results, model settings, task status
        and usage measurements. These let us perform, resume and deliver the requested work and
        enforce usage limits.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Technical records:</strong> IP address, request times, device or client information,
        request routes, response status and diagnostic/security events. Hosting and network services
        process these to deliver requests, investigate failures and prevent misuse.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Support correspondence:</strong> the address, message, attachments and other details
        you send us. Please include only information necessary for the request.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Future purchases:</strong> when Paddle checkout opens, Paddle will collect payment
        and billing details for its transactions. We may receive the account, order, subscription,
        payment-status and tax/invoice information needed to provide entitlements and support. This
        website does not currently collect payment-card details.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Paper metadata may also come from public research sources such as arXiv and OpenAlex,
      including authors, titles and abstracts. Shared material comes from the person who shares it.
      Requests to these sources can expose network information and search terms to them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where a data-protection law requires a lawful basis, account and requested-feature processing
      is necessary to provide the service under our agreement. Our legitimate interests include
      securing and maintaining the service, diagnosing failures, responding to support and improving
      the quality and reuse of standard reading results; these interests must be balanced against
      your rights. We rely on consent where required for optional processing, and on legal
      obligations where records must be retained or disclosed. Consent can be withdrawn without
      affecting earlier lawful processing.
    </p>
    <p>
      You need not supply research content to browse the website. An account identifier is needed
      for account services, and cloud AI cannot complete a task without the relevant input. AI
      answers and recommendations are assistive features; we do not use them to make decisions about
      you with legal or similarly significant effects.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="processing">
    <h2>3. Local, cloud and AI processing</h2>
    <h3>Local library and account synchronization</h3>
    <p>
      The app keeps a local library on your device. With account cloud sync enabled, supported
      library content and preferences are uploaded and synchronized between your devices. Some
      released versions enable automatic account sync by default; newer setup flows ask you to
      choose. Review your sync setting before adding restricted material. Disabling sync stops
      future automatic synchronization; it does not itself erase existing cloud copies.
    </p>
    <h3>Cloud parsing and reading tasks</h3>
    <p>
      Cloud parsing can upload PDFs to MinerU. PaperCore and custom HTTP/API (“bring your own key”
      or BYOK) close-reading tasks upload the materials needed to our server for execution, even
      with library sync disabled. Relevant content can then be sent to parsing, model and
      text-grouping providers. These jobs can continue while the app is closed, with results
      retained for later delivery.
    </p>
    <p>
      For these server-based BYOK reading jobs, the credential you supply is held in server process
      memory, not intentionally written to the job database, files or application logs. A restart
      requires the client to provide it again. This describes that execution path; it does not mean
      your device or chosen provider never stores credentials or request data.
    </p>
    <h3>Local Agents and other connected services</h3>
    <p>
      Codex and DeepSeek/DSH Agent execution is managed locally. Those tools can still send prompts
      and selected files to their providers, and authorized tools may access additional resources.
      Provider account settings, retention and any model-training controls are governed by the
      provider you select. This policy does not promise identical data practices across external
      providers.
    </p>
    <h3>Website requests and cookies</h3>
    <p>
      The interactive demo contains example content, not your research library. Your browser may
      cache website assets. Download checks may contact GitHub and our release mirror. We do not
      embed advertising trackers or marketing analytics scripts in these pages. Our hosting and
      Cloudflare network/security services can process request records and diagnostics and may use
      necessary security cookies.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="sharing">
    <h2>4. Standard readings and share links</h2>
    <p>
      Unedited, automatically generated standard reading results may be submitted to a shared
      collection for administrator quality review. Approved results can be reused by other accounts
      reading the same paper. An internal account association is retained with a submission, so this
      process should not be treated as fully anonymous. Private annotations, user-edited notes and
      independent Agent conversations are not the intended contents of that standard-reading
      collection.
    </p>
    <p>
      This review and reuse is separate from deliberately creating a share link. Do not assume that
      all generated standard reading content is restricted to your account. Contact us to object to
      processing based on legitimate interests or to request review or removal of material
      containing personal or restricted information.
    </p>
    <p>
      A share link exposes the selected fixed snapshot to people who obtain the link. The default
      expiry is 30 days; other available choices include 7 days or no expiry. You can revoke a link.
      Expiry or revocation stops further access through that link, but cannot erase downloads,
      imported copies or screenshots held by recipients.
    </p>
    <p>
      Identical stored files may be deduplicated across accounts. Removing an item from your account
      therefore does not necessarily remove a binary that another account lawfully retains. This
      storage mechanism does not give other users access to your private account records.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="providers">
    <h2>5. Service providers and other recipients</h2>
    <p>Only providers relevant to the feature or request are involved. The current service uses:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Tencent Cloud:</strong> server hosting and COS object storage for service data and
        files.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare:</strong> DNS, content delivery, network diagnostics and security for
        website/service traffic.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Our Logto-based sign-in service and Aliyun Direct Mail:</strong> authentication,
        account records and sign-in emails.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>MinerU:</strong> cloud document parsing when that parser is used.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Alibaba Cloud DashScope / Qwen and TypeSafe:</strong> configured PaperCore model
        inference and text grouping for reading tasks.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Providers you select:</strong> your custom model endpoint, OpenAI/Codex,
        DeepSeek/DSH or other connected services, according to the task and your configuration.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>GitHub:</strong> software releases and download delivery when accessed.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Paddle, once checkout is available:</strong> payment, tax, billing, fraud prevention
        and transaction support as merchant of record, under its own{' '}
        <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Authorized administrators may access information needed for support, security and
      standard-reading review. Share recipients receive the content you expose. We may also disclose
      information when legally required or necessary to protect people, investigate abuse or
      establish and defend legal claims, subject to applicable law. We do not sell personal
      information or use it for cross-context advertising.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="location">
    <h2>6. Where processing happens</h2>
    <p>
      The operator is based in Wuhan, China. Our current application hosting and COS storage are in
      Singapore. The configured DashScope endpoint processes requests in mainland China. Cloudflare
      and other external providers can process data in additional countries according to their
      infrastructure and your selected service.
    </p>
    <p>
      Using these cloud features therefore involves processing outside your country, potentially
      under different data-protection laws. We do not offer an EU-only or UK-only storage option.
      Contact us for information about a particular processing route or the transfer arrangements
      applicable to it before sending data subject to location restrictions. This notice does not
      itself constitute consent to every transfer or replace any safeguards required by applicable
      law.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="retention">
    <h2>7. Retention and deletion</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Local files:</strong> remain on your device until you remove them. Uninstalling may
        leave the chosen library folder in place.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Account and synchronized data:</strong> kept to maintain the account and library
        until deletion is requested or the data is otherwise removed under the service’s operation.
        Version history, shared files and copies referenced by other accounts can have separate
        lifetimes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Server reading jobs:</strong> completed job materials and results are normally
        scheduled for cleanup after a 30-day retention window. Copies delivered to your library,
        synchronized to your account or accepted into the shared collection are separate records and
        do not expire under that job timer.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Temporary parsing jobs:</strong> temporary server-side MinerU task records and
        materials are normally scheduled for cleanup after the configured 24-hour expiry. This is
        not a promise that every upstream provider or library copy is erased within 24 hours.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Shares:</strong> access follows the selected expiry or revocation; saved recipient
        copies are outside our direct control.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Security logs, support records and backups:</strong> retention depends on incident
        investigation, resolving support requests, recovery needs and applicable recordkeeping or
        claim requirements. There is currently no single automatic deletion period covering all
        backups. Live-record deletion does not immediately erase every historical backup.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Transaction records:</strong> if purchases become available, billing and tax records
        may need to outlast an account under applicable law and Paddle’s separate retention
        practices.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Email us for account or cloud-data deletion. We will verify the request proportionately,
      explain any necessary exceptions and handle it within the period required by applicable law.
      We may need information sufficient to identify your account; do not send passwords, API keys
      or full payment-card details.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="security">
    <h2>8. Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use HTTPS, access controls and encryption for supported server-stored data. Server-side
      encryption is not end-to-end encryption: our service holds the keys required to process that
      data, and authorized processing or administration can access it. No storage or transmission
      system can guarantee absolute security.
    </p>
    <p>
      Protect your device, sign-in email and provider credentials. Limit what you upload to what a
      task needs. If you suspect exposure of account data or a credential, contact us promptly and
      revoke the affected credential with its provider.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="rights">
    <h2>9. Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can change sync settings, choose whether to run a cloud task, choose an external provider,
      delete local content and revoke share links. These controls affect different processing paths;
      disabling one does not remove data already processed through another.
    </p>
    <p>
      Depending on applicable law, you may request access, correction, erasure, a portable copy or
      restriction of your personal information. You may withdraw consent where we rely on it.{' '}
      <strong>
        You may object to processing based on legitimate interests, including standard-reading
        quality and reuse processing.
      </strong>{' '}
      Contact <a href={`mailto:${operator.email}`}>{operator.email}</a> and describe the account and
      request.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may complain to your local data-protection authority, including the{' '}
      <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">UK Information Commissioner’s Office</a> where
      applicable. Contacting us first is optional. We do not require you to waive these rights or
      accept marketing to obtain support.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="children">
    <h2>10. Children and policy updates</h2>
    <p>
      PaperEnjoyer is intended for adults aged 18 and over. We do not knowingly offer accounts to
      children. If you believe a child’s information was provided, contact us so we can review and
      address it.
    </p>
    <p>
      We will update the date on this page when practices change and provide additional notice or
      seek consent where required. A policy update does not retrospectively authorize a new use of
      information where a separate legal basis or permission is needed.
    </p>
  </section>
</Policy>
